  "u8-l4.0.title": {
    "en": "Double negation",
    "t": "Qoʻsh inkor"
  },
  "u8-l4.0.body": {
    "en": [
      "Nikto (nobody), nič (nothing), nikdy (never), nikde and nikam (nowhere) always go with a negative verb: Nikto **ne**volal. = Nobody called.",
      "This double negative is normal Slovak, not a mistake. You can even stack them: Nikto nič **ne**robí. = Nobody does anything."
    ],
    "t": [
      "Nikto (hech kim), nič (hech narsa), nikdy (hech qachon), nikde va nikam (hech qayerda, hech qayerga) doim inkor feʼl bilan keladi: Nikto **ne**volal. = Hech kim qoʻngʻiroq qilmadi.",
      "Oʻzbek tilida ham xuddi shunday: «hech kim» + inkor feʼl. Ularni ketma-ket ham ishlatish mumkin: Nikto nič **ne**robí. = Hech kim hech narsa qilmayapti."
    ]
  },
